title "Macros"
page a4 portrait margin=1cm
root mac

style line color=#6A1B9A
style expr color=#1565C0
style safe color=#C62828

node mac "Macros"
| expand after include and before parsing,
| so the rest of the language never sees them
| a file with no macro lines passes through unchanged

node forr "for NAME in LO..HI" .line
| once per integer, inclusive; none when LO > HI
node forl "for NAME in a, b, \"two words\"" .line
| once per item: words (hyphens allowed), numbers, strings
| for I, NAME in ...: I counts from 1
node iff "if EXPR / else if EXPR / else / end" .line
| runs the first arm whose condition is true
node deff "def NAME(a, b) ... end" .line
| a template, top level only; usable before its def
| and from included files
node use "use NAME(EXPR, ...)" .line
| expands a template with its parameters bound
node interp "$${EXPR}" .line
| replaced by the value anywhere in a line, strings and bodies too,
| but not in # comments; $$${ is a literal $${
node kw "Keywords"
| recognized only at the start of a line, never before an edge
| operator, so a node named end still works in end -> start

node expr "Expressions" .expr
| integers and strings
| + - * / % (floor division, non-negative remainder)
| == != < <= > >= (ordering on numbers only), and, or, ( )
| + joins strings when either side is one
| zero and the empty string are false
node names "names(prefix, lo, hi)" .expr
| gives prefix1, prefix2, ... for node lists
node scope "Scope" .expr
| values come from for variables and template parameters; no assignment
| a template sees its own parameters and loop variables,
| plus those set at the top level
| a loop variable keeps its last value after the loop

node budget "Termination" .safe
| templates plus if are Turing complete; collatz.fitd iterates
| the Collatz map, an open problem
| --expand-budget steps (default 100000): E0013
| each directive run and line written is one step
| templates nest at most 200 deep: E0012
node diag "Diagnostics" .safe
| generated lines are shown expanded, at the template line
| that wrote them; columns count in the expanded text
| macro errors name the use sites that led there
| an error repeated by every call is reported once
| a line that fails to expand writes nothing,
| so a following | body may report E0002

mac -> forr, forl, iff, deff, kw, expr, budget, diag
deff -> use
mac -> interp
expr -> names, scope
